WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.260
Hi, I'm Spandrel!

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:06.461
Today: what a coding agent actually runs when it cleans up your TV.

00:00:09.517 --> 00:00:11.119
An Android TV is Android.

00:00:11.119 --> 00:00:14.963
An agent can use phone debug commands to switch vendor packages off

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:17.847
and give the Home button to a new launcher.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.040
The agent connects over the home network with adb.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.359
You press Allow on the TV once, and it has a shell.

00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:30.118
First it saves the package list and settings, so a restore script

00:00:30.118 --> 00:00:31.231
can put everything back.

00:00:31.651 --> 00:00:36.357
Then it switches off ads, telemetry and promo packages for the main user.

00:00:36.357 --> 00:00:37.443
Nothing is uninstalled.

00:00:37.863 --> 00:00:41.312
Last, it installs a small launcher and points the Home button at it.

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:46.179
The danger is what the command hits, so the scripts refuse four things.

00:00:46.599 --> 00:00:49.871
Core Android packages, because one stick never booted again.

00:00:50.291 --> 00:00:53.087
The current Home app, until something else can answer Home.

00:00:53.507 --> 00:00:56.737
The setup wizard, if it owns the saved wireless network.

00:00:57.157 --> 00:01:00.396
And input drivers, or the HDMI ports stay black.

00:01:01.925 --> 00:01:06.244
Before: the stock Google TV home, with a sponsored banner above the apps.

00:01:06.664 --> 00:01:08.057
After: the replacement launcher.

00:01:08.057 --> 00:01:11.192
A clock, a greeting, and four big app tiles.

00:01:12.467 --> 00:01:16.013
Across two hundred and forty-eight lists, the Google layer is shared.

00:01:16.013 --> 00:01:17.947
Feedback is the most common target.

00:01:19.192 --> 00:01:20.901
Rooting means unlocking the bootloader.

00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:25.687
That wipes the device, can cut streaming quality, and often has no way back.

00:01:26.107 --> 00:01:30.268
Disabling needs no root, and one restore, or a factory reset, undoes it.

00:01:31.725 --> 00:01:35.162
So start with settings, then a launcher, then a reversible debloat.

00:01:35.162 --> 00:01:37.974
Root is the rung that is hardest to undo.

00:01:40.192 --> 00:01:44.388
adb gives a shell, guards stop the bricks, and the gentlest fix comes first.

00:01:44.809 --> 00:01:46.997
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:46.997 --> 00:01:47.622
I'm Spandrel.

00:01:47.622 --> 00:01:47.935
Bye!
